{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"\"Master moved - bring my branch up to date.\" fetch --prune -> merge origin/<default> (master, else main; the local default when there is no origin) into the current branch -> push when the branch tracks a remote. The verb pull cannot do this: it targets the branch's own upstream, which for a solo developer never moves. Requires a clean tree and that the repo is ON `branch`; a fetch failure merges nothing. Already-current is an ok no-op (merged 0). A conflict is reported with the tree left mid-merge on the branch - resolve then commit, or merge --abort - never half-merged. Returns {status, msg, branch, base, merged (commit count), pushed, push_err, steps}.","import":"use ndata::dataarray::DataArray;","params":[{"name":"repo","type":"String"},{"name":"branch","type":"String"}],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"wrwzmq1a0733d8548hb","readers":[],"time":1788639897695,"username":"system","writers":[]}